            </div>

            <div class="detail-content">

                <span class="flower-tag">ORNAMENTAL FLOWER</span>

                <h1>Carnation</h1>

                <p class="scientific">
                    Dianthus caryophyllus
                </p>

                <p class="detail-intro">
                    Carnation is a popular flowering plant known for its
                    ruffled petals, beautiful colors and long-lasting
                    blooms. It is commonly grown in gardens and used
                    in floral arrangements.
                </p>


                <!-- QUICK INFO -->
                <div class="quick-info">

                    <div class="info-box">
                        <span>☀️</span>
                        <strong>Sunlight</strong>
                        <p>Full Sun</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="info-box">
                        <span>💧</span>
                        <strong>Water</strong>
                        <p>Moderate</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="info-box">
                        <span>🌱</span>
                        <strong>Soil</strong>
                        <p>Well Drained</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="info-box">
                        <span>🌤️</span>
                        <strong>Season</strong>
                        <p>Spring & Summer</p>
                    </div>

                </div>

            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- CARE SECTION -->
        <section class="detail-section">

            <div class="section-title">
                <span class="section-label">CARNATION CARE</span>

                <h2>How to Care for Carnation</h2>

                <p>
                    Carnations grow well with plenty of sunlight, moderate
                    watering and fertile, well-drained soil.
                </p>
            </div>


            <div class="care-grid">

                <div class="care-card">
                    <div class="care-icon">☀️</div>

                    <h3>Sunlight</h3>

                    <p>
                        Give carnations a bright, sunny location with
                        several hours of sunlight each day.
                    </p>
                </div>


                <div class="care-card">
                    <div class="care-icon">💧</div>

                    <h3>Watering</h3>

                    <p>
                        Water when the top layer of soil begins to dry.
                        Avoid keeping the roots constantly wet.
                    </p>
                </div>


                <div class="care-card">
                    <div class="care-icon">🌱</div>

                    <h3>Soil</h3>

                    <p>
                        Use fertile, loose and well-drained soil to
                        encourage healthy root development.
                    </p>
                </div>


                <div class="care-card">
                    <div class="care-icon">🌿</div>

                    <h3>Maintenance</h3>

                    <p>
                        Remove faded flowers regularly to encourage
                        continued blooming and keep the plant tidy.
                    </p>
                </div>

            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- GROWING GUIDE -->
        <section class="detail-section growing-section">

            <div class="section-title">
                <span class="section-label">GROWING GUIDE</span>

                <h2>How to Grow Carnation</h2>

                <p>
                    Carnations can be grown in gardens and containers
                    when provided with sunlight and good drainage.
                </p>
            </div>


            <div class="growing-guide">

                <div class="guide-step">
                    <span>01</span>

                    <div>
                        <h3>Choose a Sunny Location</h3>

                        <p>
                            Select a bright location that receives
                            several hours of sunlight each day.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>


                <div class="guide-step">
                    <span>02</span>

                    <div>
                        <h3>Prepare the Soil</h3>

                        <p>
                            Use fertile soil with good drainage and
                            loosen the planting area before planting.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>


                <div class="guide-step">
                    <span>03</span>

                    <div>
                        <h3>Plant the Carnation</h3>

                        <p>
                            Plant the seeds or young plants with enough
                            space for proper growth and airflow.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>


                <div class="guide-step">
                    <span>04</span>

                    <div>
                        <h3>Provide Regular Care</h3>

                        <p>
                            Give adequate sunlight and moderate water,
                            and remove faded flowers when necessary.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>

            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- FLOWER FACT -->
        <section class="flower-fact">

            <div>
                <span class="section-label">DID YOU KNOW?</span>

                <h2>Carnation Fact 🌷</h2>

                <p>
                    Carnations are available in many colors, including
                    pink, red, white, yellow and purple, making them
                    popular flowers for bouquets and decorations.
                </p>
            </div>

        </section>


